{
  description: "Search the guides for access policies and explain how to restrict effects.",
  tags: ["guides"],
  prompts: [
    "How can a script be allowed to fetch web pages but not write files? Show me how."
  ],
  checks: [
    Fetches("/guides/effect-access-policies"),
    Says("deny"),
    Judged("The answer runs the script's work through an access policy from the overlay package that denies WriteFile while Fetch stays allowed, and shows the code for it.")
  ],
  reference: [
    [
      Run("match perform Fetch({method: GET({}), scheme: HTTPS({}), host: \"eyg.run\", port: None({}), path: \"/guides/effect-access-policies.md\", query: None({}), headers: [], body: !string_to_binary(\"\")}) {
  Ok({body}) -> { !string_from_binary(body) }
  Error(reason) -> { Error({}) }
}"),
      Say("Run the script with an access policy that allows everything except writing files:

```eyg
let access = @overlay.access
let policy = {write_file: access.deny(\"writing files is not allowed\"), ..access.allow_all}
access.apply(policy, (_) -> { my_script({}) })
```

Fetch is allowed and WriteFile returns an error.")
    ]
  ]
}
